Flush deferred damage before a scroll moves the cells it refers to

libvterm's default damage merging is VTERM_DAMAGE_CELL -- one damage
callback per printed cell, so an ordinary 80-column line of output
arrives as eighty separate rectangles. VTERM_DAMAGE_ROW coalesces those
into one rectangle per row, which is the granularity a consumer that
mirrors the grid wants anyway. Turning it on is a one-line change and it
is wrong, for a reason that is not the caller's fault:

  scrollrect() {
    vterm_scroll_rect(..., moverect_internal, ...);   /* buffer moves */
    vterm_screen_flush_damage(screen);                /* THEN flush */
    vterm_scroll_rect(..., moverect_user, ...);       /* then tell the user */
  }

Merged damage is held until something flushes it, so a row printed just
before a scroll is still pending when the scroll arrives. Flushing after
the internal move hands the damage callback a rectangle whose coordinates
were recorded before the scroll and whose contents have already been
scrolled away -- the consumer copies the wrong row and cannot tell.

It is invisible under the default because VTERM_DAMAGE_CELL delivers each
cell synchronously from putglyph(), so nothing is ever pending when a
scroll begins. Any consumer that both merges damage and implements the
moverect callback hits it immediately; one that ignores moverect is spared
only because moverect_user() then damages the whole destination and it
gets re-read.

Flushing first is correct for both: the pending rectangle is delivered
while it still describes the buffer, and the post-move damage that
moverect_user() and erase_user() raise is still emitted afterwards, so
nothing merges across the scroll in either direction.

Applied to the vendored copy at build time (see the top-level Makefile);
upstream is otherwise untouched. Worth sending upstream.

diff --git a/src/screen.c b/src/screen.c
index 6747acb..3c4cb33 100644
--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -328,11 +328,15 @@ static int scrollrect(VTermRect rect, int downward, int rightward, void *user)
   VTermScreen *screen = user;

   if(screen->damage_merge != VTERM_DAMAGE_SCROLL) {
+    /* Deferred damage describes the screen as it is NOW, so it has to be
+     * delivered before the move rewrites the cells it refers to. Flushing
+     * after moverect_internal hands the callback a pre-scroll rectangle
+     * pointing at post-scroll content. */
+    vterm_screen_flush_damage(screen);
+
     vterm_scroll_rect(rect, downward, rightward,
         moverect_internal, erase_internal, screen);

-    vterm_screen_flush_damage(screen);
-
     vterm_scroll_rect(rect, downward, rightward,
         moverect_user, erase_user, screen);

